@startuml UC-002-analysis-sequence
!include ../../../diagrams/style.iuml
title UC-002 Prepare benchmark dataset: analysis sequence diagram

actor Developer
boundary "Command Line" as CLI
control "Prepare Benchmark" as Prep
boundary "Benchmark File Reader" as BFR
database "Benchmark file" as File
entity "Problem List" as PL
entity "Test Case" as TC
entity "Benchmark" as B
entity "Benchmark Error" as BE

note over CLI, Prep
  Triggered at the start of a run (UC-006),
  before any model is called.
end note

Developer -> CLI : run evaluation (UC-006)
CLI -> Prep : load benchmark(path)
Prep -> BFR : read text(path)
BFR -> File : read
alt 1a: the file is missing
  File --> BFR : not found
  BFR --> Prep : file not found
  Prep -> BE : create(path, the one problem)
  Prep --> CLI : error(path, the one problem)
else the file reads
  File --> BFR : content
  BFR --> Prep : file content
  Prep -> Prep : parse content as JSON
  alt 2a, 2b: invalid JSON, or the top level is not an object
    Prep -> BE : create(path, the one problem)
    Prep --> CLI : error(path, the one problem)
  else the content parses to an object
    Prep -> Prep : check benchmark id, name,\nand that cases is a non-empty list
    opt 3a, 3b: id or name blank, cases missing or empty
      Prep -> PL : add problem, with its location
    end
    loop for each case, in file order
      Prep -> Prep : check it is an object with three\nnon-empty text fields and no others
      alt 4a, 4b, 4c: not an object, a field missing or blank, or an unknown field
        Prep -> PL : add problem, with its location
      else the case is usable
        Prep -> TC : create(id, question, expected answer)
        Prep -> Prep : check the id is not used by an earlier case
        opt 4d: the id duplicates an earlier case's id
          Prep -> PL : add problem, with its location
        end
      end
    end
    Prep -> PL : any problems?
    alt main success scenario: no problems
      PL --> Prep : none
      Prep -> B : create(id, name, test cases in file order)
      Prep --> CLI : benchmark(id, name, test cases in file order)
    else 3a, 3b, 4a to 4d: the content breaks one or more rules
      PL --> Prep : problems, in file order
      Prep -> BE : create(path, every problem)
      Prep --> CLI : error(path, every problem, in file order)
    end
  end
end

note right of PL
  Each broken rule adds a problem with its
  location, and checking goes on. At the end,
  any problem means a Benchmark Error listing
  them all, and no Benchmark (AC-002-08).
end note
note over CLI, Prep
  Business rule: no model is called for a
  benchmark that fails to load.
end note
@enduml
